    summary_en: "An operation led by INTERPOL, named 'Operation Ramz,' successfully dismantled a phishing-as-a-service (Phishing-as-a-Service, PhaaS) platform called Sniper Dz. This platform has been active since at least 2015, providing cybercriminals with a complete phishing toolkit, hosting infrastructure, and operational support. According to Group-IB's analysis, Sniper Dz collected over 45,000 victim records and targeted 30 major global organizations, including PayPal, Facebook, Instagram, Yahoo, Netflix, and Steam. The platform utilized 80 phishing templates, impersonating well-known brands and government agencies to steal account credentials and personal sensitive data. Beyond traditional credential theft, attackers also employed social engineering, impersonating celebrity accounts for fraud. This operation resulted in the arrest of 201 suspects in the MENA region, along with the seizure of related equipment and phishing scripts. This incident serves as a warning to the industry to heighten vigilance, especially regarding phishing attacks that impersonate well-known brands or celebrities, and to strengthen employee cybersecurity awareness.",
