    title_en: "Europol successfully dismantles cryptocurrency laundering service AudiA6, cutting off criminal group funding channels",
    summary_en: "The European law enforcement agency Europol announced the successful dismantling of a cryptocurrency laundering service named AudiA6. Since its activation in 2021, the platform has been used to launder hundreds of millions of euros in illicit proceeds, becoming a central hub for ransomware and cybercrime groups. The operation involved the arrest of two suspects and multiple searches in locations including Georgia, resulting in the seizure of over 30 servers and vast amounts of cryptocurrency assets. Investigations revealed that AudiA6 was an industrial-scale laundering operation, relying on thousands of fake exchange accounts opened using stolen identities. Law enforcement noted that criminal groups are increasingly depending on platforms like \"mixer-as-a-service\" to quickly transfer illicit cryptocurrencies into the digital underworld, bypassing anti-money laundering controls. The success of this operation is attributed to prior investigations by Polish police into the suspects, completed in cooperation with international partners such as the U.S. Department of Justice (DoJ).",
