    summary_en: "Multiple major Linux distributions (including AlmaLinux, Debian, Fedora, Mageia, Red Hat, SUSE, and Ubuntu) have recently released extensive security updates. This update covers a wide range, affecting core system components, application libraries, and server software. Affected components include, but are not limited to: the Linux kernel, OpenSSL, glibc, samba, Nginx, Apache2, various .NET versions (such as .NET 8.0, .NET 10.0), Redis, and various container tools (such as buildah, podman). Each distribution has applied independent patches for different product lines; for example, SUSE updated gnutls, openssh, and webkit2gtk3; and Red Hat updated buildah, podman, and skopeo. In practice, system administrators should immediately check and update all affected components to patch potential vulnerabilities, ensuring system stability and security. Due to the extensive scope of the updates, it is recommended to perform phased, validated upgrades based on the official security announcements of each distribution.",
