    title_en: "iOS 27 Find My Feature Upgrade: Adds Privacy Controls, Allows Location Hiding Without Notification",
    summary_en: "Apple has significantly updated the \"Find My\" application in iOS 27, focusing on enhancing user privacy controls. Key new features include more flexible location sharing options, allowing users to set custom durations or specific end dates for sharing, and the ability to temporarily pause sharing. Most notable is that users can now \"hide their location\" from specific individuals without them receiving any notification or alert. When a user pauses or stops sharing their location, the recipient will see a \"No Location Found\" message in the Find My app. Additionally, the Find My interface has been updated with a \"Liquid Glass\" style, allowing the main page to display more precise geographical location information directly, without needing to tap individual cards. These updates aim to give users more granular location management capabilities while improving the overall user experience of the application.",
