    id: "20260612-045",
    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Android",
    title: "Android WebView 處理不當：Groww 應用程式面臨未經授權的 URL 處理漏洞",
    summary: "本漏洞（CVE-2026-12065）影響在 Android 平台上運行的 Groww 股票、基金和黃金應用程式，特別是其 WebView URL Handler 組件。該漏洞的本質在於對自定義 URL Scheme 的處理缺乏適當的授權檢查，可能導致在應用程式內執行未經授權的行為。攻擊者若能利用此缺陷，可能在實體設備上發動攻擊。雖然攻擊的複雜度被評估為較高，但漏洞利用程式碼已公開，存在被利用的風險。建議用戶和開發者應密切關注相關的修補公告，並確保應用程式使用最新的、安全加固的 WebView 組件版本，以防止未經授權的 URL 處理。",
    tags: ["Android", "WebView", "Groww", "CVE-2026-12065", "URL Handler", "資安"],
    title_en: "Android WebView Improper Handling: Groww Application Faces Unauthorized URL Processing Vulnerability",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability (CVE-2026-12065) affects the Groww stock, fund, and gold application running on the Android platform, specifically its WebView URL Handler component. The core issue lies in the lack of proper authorization checks when handling custom URL Schemes, which could potentially lead to unauthorized actions being executed within the application. If an attacker can exploit this flaw, they may launch an attack on a physical device. Although the complexity of the attack is assessed as high, exploit code has been made public, posing a risk of exploitation. Users and developers are advised to closely monitor relevant patch announcements and ensure the application uses the latest, security-hardened WebView component version to prevent unauthorized URL processing.",
