    category: "重點關注",
    title: "Google 對利用 Gemini 進行金融詐騙的網路犯罪組織提起訴訟，呼籲制定 AI 時代的嚴格法規",
    summary: "Google 已對一個基於中國的網路犯罪組織「Outsider Enterprise」提起訴訟。該組織據稱利用 Gemini 模型，大規模發送金融詐騙，目標是數十萬美國受害者，造成數百萬美元的損失。犯罪集團利用 AI 技術，創建了模仿 Google、YouTube、美國郵政服務及紐約 E-ZPass 等政府機構的假網站，並生成了超過 100 萬個詐騙 URL。此外，該組織在兩週內向 Android 用戶發送了 250 萬條包含連結的訊息，並發送了 55,000 條垃圾簡訊。Google 不僅透過法律途徑行動，也正與美國主要電信業者和 FBI 協調，以阻擋詐騙簡訊。此事件凸顯了 AI 技術的雙面性，促使 Google 積極推動更貼合 AI 時代的法律規範，以應對日益嚴重的 AI 驅動的網路犯罪。",
    tags: ["Google", "Gemini", "AI 詐騙", "網路犯罪", "Outsider Enterprise", "法規監管"],
    title_en: "Google Sues Cybercrime Group for Using Gemini in Financial Scams, Calls for Strict AI-Era Regulations",
    summary_en: "Google has filed a lawsuit against a China-based cybercrime organization called \"Outsider Enterprise.\" The group is alleged to have used the Gemini model to send large-scale financial scams, targeting hundreds of thousands of American victims and causing millions of dollars in losses. The criminal group utilized AI technology to create fake websites mimicking institutions such as Google, YouTube, the U.S. Postal Service, and the New York E-ZPass, and generated over 1 million scam URLs. Furthermore, the organization sent 2.5 million messages containing links to Android users within two weeks, along with 55,000 spam SMS messages. Google is taking action not only through legal means but is also coordinating with major U.S. telecommunications carriers and the FBI to block the scam messages. This incident highlights the dual nature of AI technology, prompting Google to actively advocate for legal standards better suited for the AI era to combat increasingly severe AI-driven cybercrime.",
    tags_en: ["Google", "Gemini", "AI Scams", "Cybercrime", "Outsider Enterprise", "Regulation"],
    sources: [
      { name: "9to5Google", url: "https://9to5google.com/2026/06/12/google-sues-cybercrime-network-that-used-gemini-for-financial-scams", lang: "EN" }
    ]
