    title_en: "Ivanti Sentry Critical Vulnerability Alert: OS Command Injection and Authentication Bypass, Immediate Patching Recommended",
    summary_en: "Security vendor Ivanti has released a security update for its Ivanti Sentry product, which is used to secure corporate mobile device communications, addressing multiple critical vulnerabilities. The affected vulnerabilities include CVE-2026-10520 (Operating System Command Injection) and CVE-2026-10523 (Authentication Bypass). CVE-2026-10520 allows unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary system commands with root privileges via specially crafted requests. Meanwhile, CVE-2026-10523 allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass authentication, create arbitrary administrative accounts, and gain full system administrative privileges. The CVSS v3.1 scores for these vulnerabilities are 10 and 9.9, respectively. Affected product versions include Ivanti Sentry versions below 10.5.2, below 10.6.2, and below 10.7.1. All users and administrators are advised to immediately update the affected product to the latest version to prevent malicious exploitation.",
